    "prompt": "Inspect this ordered set of underwater research images. In each image locate every clearly visible individual animal. Look for small animals. Use the tightest plausible box around each visible animal. Leave geological features, vegetation and equipment out. Use only these ecological groups: Demersal (bottom-associated fish and other swimmers), Motile Epifauna (animals moving on the seafloor), Planktonic (drifting in the water column), Sessile Epifauna (attached animals), or Unresolved (visible animal, group uncertain). For each image return its integer frame index and objects. Each object must have label and bbox_2d [left,top,right,bottom] in coordinates 0 to 1000 relative to that image. Do not invent occluded objects or a box spanning multiple animals. For an empty frame return an empty objects array. Return JSON only: {\"frames\":[{\"frame\":0,\"objects\":[{\"label\":\"Demersal\",\"bbox_2d\":[12,124,41,180]}]}]}.",
